DSStats no longer crashes on a DERIVE sample after an unknown one, keeps negative and unknown statistics instead of storing 0, reads each RRDtool response to its status line, reads period statistics from the finest RRA that covers the period, processes each data source once across parallel and Boost workers, names and selects partitions by ISO week and the requested time, clears stale hourly averages, writes in full batches, and waits for RRDtool without spinning
